pert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "North Dakota sits among the most Republican states in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly 18 points to the right of the country. The incumbent president is term-limited, making this an open race, but no state polls, expert ratings, or prediction-market pricing are available for it. The forecast therefore rests on fundamentals, which point firmly to the Republican ticket.\n\nRecent cycles show the state backing Republicans by double digits at the presidential level regardless of national conditions, and nothing in current coverage suggests an unusual environment. Uncertainty is wider than usual because direct polling is absent, but a shift large enough to put North Dakota in contention would require a national swing far beyond what the evidence now shows. The practical question is the size of the Republican margin rather than the winner, and the rating is Safe Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0273, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0549, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0572, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0505, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0515, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0556, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0598, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0528, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0566, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.05, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.052, "margin": -18.0}]}